PX Password Strength
====================

Visual overlay for the Roundcube `password` plugin. Adds a live password
strength bar and requirements checklist to Settings → Password.

Features
--------
- Strength bar (weak / medium / strong) updated as user types.
- Checklist of password rules (length, lower, upper, digit, special, diacritics).
- Auto-configures `password_strength_driver=px_strength` if not explicitly set.
- Hides native `password` plugin rules list to avoid duplicate UI.

Installation
------------
1. Enable plugin in `config/config.inc.php` (after `password`):

   $config['plugins'] = [..., 'password', 'px_password_strength'];

2. Copy config template (optional):

   cp plugins/px_password_strength/config.inc.php.dist plugins/px_password_strength/config.inc.php

Password policy
---------------
Local policy keys in `config.inc.php`:
- `px_password_strength_minimum_length` (default: 8)
- `px_password_strength_require_lower` / `_upper` / `_digit` / `_special`
- `px_password_strength_forbid_diacritics`

Shared/global override (set in `config/config.inc.php`):
- `px_password_policy_minimum_length`
- `px_password_policy_require_lower` / `_upper` / `_digit` / `_special`
- `px_password_policy_forbid_diacritics`

When global keys are set, they override local keys for both
`px_password_strength` and `px_password_recovery`.

Key options
-----------
| Option | Default | Description |
|--------|---------|-------------|
| `px_password_strength_enabled` | `true` | Master switch |
| `px_password_strength_hide_native_rules` | `true` | Hide native `#ruleslist` |
| `px_password_strength_show_strength_label` | `true` | Show text label on bar |
| `px_password_strength_minimum_length` | `8` | Minimum password length |

Notes
-----
- This plugin is primarily a visual overlay. Server-side validation is still
  handled by the `password` plugin and its configured driver.
- If `password_strength_driver` is unset, the plugin auto-sets it to
  `px_strength` with `password_minimum_score=2`.
- When local or shared minimum length is configured, the plugin exposes
  the effective value to the `password` plugin backend (`password_minimum_length`).
